# Context

## Background
An external review of 0b22357 reported both defects as source-level
findings and said it had not reproduced them end to end. A ten-agent
verification pass confirmed each claim against HEAD; four adversarial
refuters could not overturn either one. Two regression tests were
added first and failed before the fix.

## Why This Way
Evaluating siblings instead of rejecting $ref-with-siblings follows
the class contract: the validator declares a Draft 2020-12 subset
(validator.ts header, SPEC section 23.5), and 2020-12 made $ref an
applicator that applies beside siblings. Rejecting the combination
would refuse valid OpenAPI 3.1 documents.

## Gotchas
- The OpenAPI compiler (packages/openapi/src/normalize.ts) inlines
  non-cyclic refs and merges siblings, which masked the $ref defect
  for compiled documents. Cyclic refs keep the $ref form and were
  exposed, as was every direct SchemaValidator use.
- codePointLength counts surrogate pairs in a loop instead of
  Array.from or a /./gu match so a large body string validates
  without an allocation proportional to its length.

## Related
